# Content pipeline — stage mapping

See `PROJECT.md` §2 for the full table.

## Stage 6 (current) — Dzen + quality

After images/links: optional detectors (scores only), optional Humanizer
rewrite, optional summary, then a shorter Dzen version of the **same**
article from its title (`use_dzen`). Three Dzen image slots: cover + two
in the body.

Do not pull CMS, GPTZero/Copyscape HTTP, or third-party Humanizer SaaS
into this work.

## Stage 5 — Images + internal linking

After writer / multi-agent editor: replace image placeholders via `ImageProvider`.
Hero `COVER_PLACEHOLDER` → `images/cover.png` is generated from the **title**.
In-body photos use the **section heading + excerpt**.
Then insert markdown links to other completed articles (no extra LLM).
When competitor research is on, photo counts per outline block come from
the average of competitor `section_images`.

## Stage 4 — Multi-agent

Research → SEO → Writer → Fact Checker → Editor (`use_multi_agent`).

## Topic Discovery (sibling of Stage 3)

Seeds → Google + Yandex SERP snapshots (official APIs, not HTML scrape) →
dedupe → TopicPlanner briefs → `topics.json` → existing generate.

Does not replace Stage 3 research (that still analyzes an already chosen topic).

## Competitor topic files (first substep of competitor analysis)

xlsx/csv/txt dumps → `app/core/competitor_sources.py` → `ContentGapAnalyst` →
`content-plan` rows → `app/core/competitor_plan.py` → `topics/*.json`.
Ready `content-plan-*.json` skips the analyst. Discovery stays a sibling
(search seeds). Stage 3 research is the second substep (outline for a chosen
topic). Do not ingest the topic table into RAG; project context lives in a
local `knowledge/<project>-brief.md` (not committed).

## Stage 3 — Research / SEO / competitors

Topic → SERP TOP articles → structure parse → improved outline → generate.

## Stage 2 — Knowledge Base / RAG

Documents → parser → chunking → embeddings → pgvector → optional context on generate.

## Stage 1 — keep this

- **4** Image/infographic **placeholders** in writer prompts (Stage 5 replaces them when `use_images`)
- **5** `title`, `meta_description`, `url_slug` — prompt rules + persisted fields (Stage 3 strengthens them from SERP)
- **10** Callouts: Совет / Важно / Подсказка / Лайфхак / Рекомендация (prompt; only where natural)
- Basic generation from brief / `outline` (manual outline in `topics.json` is OK when research is off)

## Stage 3 — in scope

- **1** TOP competitor articles
- **2** Competitor structure → improved outline
- **3** Generate article **from that** competitor-based structure

## Stage 5 — in scope

- **4** real images for `IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_N` / `INFOGRAPHIC_PLACEHOLDER_N`
- **7** Internal linking between completed articles

## Stage 6 — in scope

- **6** Dzen: shorter same-article version, 3 images (cover + two in body)
- **8** Detectors + optional Humanizer (own chat; not Copyscape / GPTZero / SaaS)
- **9** Summary from the final markdown (before CMS)

## Later

CMS / review / publish is **Stage 8**, after images, links and quality checks.
Analytics is **Stage 9** (after publication). n8n HTML packaging is **Stage 7**.

Deferred (do not implement without an explicit task):

- **Operator UI (Stage 8a)** — F0–F5 done, including `review_status`.
  CMS publish stays Stage 8. Plan:
  `PROJECT.md` §15 «План: операторский UI» and `GUIDE.md` §5.7 / §11.Д.
- **Multiple projects** — done (P0–P5). KB, topics, articles, research, and
 internal links stay inside one `project_id`. Do not mix RAG or internal
 links across projects. Auth/billing stay out.

Topic source switch is implemented: `scripts/build_topics.py --mode discovery|competitor`
(Makefile `topics-discovery` / `topics-competitors`). Not a generate flag, not
a unified FastAPI orchestrator, not n8n.

## Do not

- Pull Humanizer SaaS, GPTZero/Copyscape, or CMS into this work without an explicit assignment. CMS is Stage 8 (after images and quality).
- Replace Markdown storage with HTML-only or image-only flows.
